          "date": "2026-10-30 20:01:08.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: time rpc.sh phases",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: time rpc.sh phases\n\nTiming trace only, do not land. An rpc.sh call costs 1.8 to\n2.7 seconds before its command runs on Maloo, against about\n0.4 seconds on an idle local VM, and it is not known why.\n\nEach call writes one tagged line of phase timestamps to the\nkernel log on its node. One call in 20 also runs under xtrace\nand reports the time spent per file, per command and on its\nslowest lines. Sampled calls are marked so that they can be\nleft out of the phase means.\n\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-sec\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly testlist=sanity-lnet\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I58cb0c416c73218db6d04403ae2fcfd6bd887158\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
